{
  "$comment": "Every method+path route the app serves, as a checkable claim. This is the COVERAGE inventory, not a config: `tools/route-coverage.mjs` walks it against a live server and asserts each route is reachable, so a route that stops being served fails the gate. Since tb-0030 step 6 deleted the `_app/route.ts` dispatcher, the routes ARE the folders under `ahscripts/routes/` - the paths below mirror that tree, with `{param}` matching a `{param}` folder and a placeholder id substituted at probe time - and an entry is added or removed in the SAME commit as its folder. `probe` says how to reach it: `auth` whether a session is needed, `body` a form body for POST/DELETE, and `expect` the statuses that count as reachable (anything else is a failure). A route that is intentionally unroutable says so in `note`.",
