  "id_substitute_note": "Every {id} / {lineId} substitute is a real UUIDv7 (48-bit unix-ms | version 7 | variant 10) in base64, and exists in no row. Two earlier substitutes were wrong in ways that made the gate report defects that were not there: the literal string does-not-exist is not valid base64 at all, so b64ToHex threw; and Buffer.alloc(16,1) IS valid base64 but NOT a valid UUIDv7, so the invoice_lock CHECK (is_uuid_v7) rejected it and eight invoice write routes answered an opaque 500. A probe id has to be well-formed all the way down, or the gate tests the codec instead of the route."
}
